IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `soga-buyers`

-- Sale of Goods Act 1979, ss 6, 14, 15A, 18, 20, 21, 23, 30, 35, 50, 51, 53 and 57 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_sale-of-goods-act-1979.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a shop sale with a hidden defect` MEANS Purchase WITH
    `the seller sells in the course of a business` IS TRUE
    `a business agent sells for a private owner` IS FALSE
    `the buyer knew or was told the owner was private` IS FALSE
    `the defect was drawn to the buyer's attention before the contract` IS FALSE
    `the buyer examined the goods before the contract` IS FALSE
    `that examination ought to have revealed the defect` IS FALSE
    `the buyer made a particular purpose known` IS FALSE
    `the buyer did not or could not reasonably rely on the seller` IS FALSE
    `the seller has shown the buyer does not deal as consumer` IS FALSE
    `the seller has shown the breach is so slight that rejection is unreasonable` IS FALSE
    `the buyer has accepted the goods` IS FALSE

